<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Infographic illustrating the process of human-robot interaction leading to social carry-over and ethical risk. Step one describes initial encounters with robots via anthropomorphic cues, agency attribution, embodied interaction, and situated conceptualizations. Step two shows interactional learning, functional social responsiveness, repeated exchanges, and predictions. Step three highlights how social expectations from these interactions influence later human-human interaction, increasing totalization risks and reducing ethical responsiveness. Arrows and simple figures depict the flow, with a note that meeting moments can challenge ethical risk.) /K 245 0 R /P 58 0 R /Pg 9 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
